        "date": "2026-11-08T19:22:23Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a non-finite work-offset placement by name\n\nA work offset whose rotation quaternion carried NaN or infinite parts\n(or a zero norm) fell through the #315 rotated-offset gate as\n\"unrotated\", so it would post as if the offset had no rotation.\n\n- posting: one classifier (offset_frame: Square / Rotated / NonFinite)\n  feeds the gate; a non-finite origin or rotation is refused with its\n  own named line.\n- SetWcsOrigin: its non-finite / degenerate refusals now name the slot.\n- project load: a WCS row with a non-finite or zero-norm placement is\n  refused by name instead of landing as the identity.\n- setup sheet: a rotated (or non-finite) offset states it under the\n  offset line; unrotated offsets render byte-identical.\n\nPinned by tests/rotated_wcs.rs.\n\nFixes #327\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
